# Portable artifact routing bundle

This directory is the project-owned source of truth for artifact location and
format. It remains readable after any setup tool or plugin has been removed.

## Read in this order

1. `artifact-routing.json` identifies the project mode, applications, ownership
   roots and the two host-local adapter states.
2. `artifact-format-contract.json` defines the required metadata and path rules
   for a generated artifact.
3. The application routing instruction at `{{ROUTING_INSTRUCTION}}` is the
   detailed, app-scoped routing authority.

## Host-local adapters

The shared bundle is under `.docs/harness/`; host-local files are intentionally
separate:

- Claude: `.claude/settings.json` and `.claude/hooks/claude-pre-tool-use.ps1`
- Codex: `.codex/hooks.json` and `.codex/hooks/codex-pre-tool-use.ps1`

Both remain `pending-trust` until an administrator approves host installation
and the host-specific trust step. `install-routing.ps1 -Plan` is safe to run:
it emits the identical proposed local targets and does not write files.

## Recovery and review

Do not copy an adapter or configuration from one host to the other. Inspect the
host-specific input contract in its adapter, review the plan, then apply the
approved host-specific merge workflow. A proposal from `.docs/_inbox/` remains
non-canonical until its provenance and target path are explicitly approved.
